.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="In the Bronsted-Lowry picture an acid is a proton donor and its deprotonated form is a conjugate base -- itself a genuine base that accepts a proton from water. For every pair, K_aK_b = K_w, so the stronger the acid, the weaker its conjugate base. Here the acetate ion is modelled as a base in its own right with WeakBase (K_b = K_w/K_a), alongside acetic acid as WeakAcid, and several conjugate pairs are placed on the line pK_a + pK_b = 14.">

